# The gate's own configuration, pinned (fnd §3.6, FND-08; ARCH-gate-config in
# tools/jfl-architecture/src/gate.rs): one SHA-256 per justfile recipe of the gate, the
# justfile's top-level lines, the xtask composition (tools/xtask/Cargo.toml and every file of
# tools/xtask/src: the stage catalog, each stage's command and the preflight; XT-01) and its
# launcher (scripts/xtask.sh), each script the gate runs (every scripts/test-*.sh included), the
# policies a stage reads by path (.github/zizmor.yml, deny.toml) and the tool pins (mise.toml,
# mise.lock, tools/versions.toml; XT-02; every file under .mise/, the npm
# tools' locked graphs; FORMAL-01), what decides landing (scripts/land.sh, scripts/dco-check.sh) and the session
# hooks (.claude/hooks/session-start.sh, stop-gate.sh; FND-09). A change to any of them fails the
# architecture stage until its line here changes in the same commit, so the gate cannot be
# neutered without a visible edit of this file; review reads every changed line as a change of
# the gate itself. The failure names the line to write.
